You are given a task to integrate a component from the **kinetik** motion library into this codebase.

# Announcement Banner (`banner-announcement`)

Top-of-page announcement bar: a sheen sweeps across, several messages rotate vertically (paused on hover/focus), the arrow nudges on hover, and dismissal collapses the bar and is remembered.

## What it should do
Build an announcement bar: dark full-width strip with a CSS gradient sheen sweeping across, a message link (optional pill label + arrow that nudges on hover) that rotates vertically between items with AnimatePresence popLayout, pausing on hover/focus. Dismiss collapses height to 0 and stores a flag in localStorage.

## Project requirements
- React 19 + TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4, shadcn/ui-style CSS variables (`background`, `foreground`, `muted`, `muted-foreground`, `border`, `card`, `primary`, `ring`). If the project lacks shadcn, set it up first (`npx shadcn@latest init`).
- Animation engine: **motion**.
- Install dependencies: `npm i motion lucide-react`
- Put the component at `components/kinetik/banner-announcement.tsx`.
- `cn` lives at `lib/kinetik/utils.ts` (source below).
- Shared hooks go at `lib/kinetik/core.ts` (source below).
- Motion tokens go at `lib/kinetik/tokens.ts` (source below). Use tokens instead of magic numbers.

## Non-negotiables
- **Accessibility:** Labelled region; rotation pauses on hover and focus; dismiss is a labelled button and persists. Reduced motion: no sheen, crossfades.
- **Performance:** CSS sheen; one interval; height animation only on dismiss.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` (replace movement with opacity or an instant change).
- Animate only transform / opacity / filter / clip-path. No hard-coded theme colors — use CSS variables so it works in light and dark.

